From 17ce95dc568d346fe072882199fbe2f5b993a0ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jingze Ma <jingzema0211@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:04:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] rad_m1: default initialisers for every scalar member;
 CleanFaceVector reads x2f(j+1) only off the theta faces

The scalar members of RadiationM1 without an initialiser (bool, int, Real, arrays;
247 declaration lines) take {} : a member that only one code path sets (VetInit,
ImplicitInit, the partition or halo setup, ...) now reads as zero/false on the others
on every backend, as it did on a CPU's fresh pages (vet_milne, 073378e14, was one).
Hydro::wb_option takes isodensity (0) for the same reason (read by the flux kernels
without wb_dynamic; UBSan: load of an invalid WBOption).  CleanFaceVector: a theta
face reads no x2f(m,j+1) (out of range at the high face of a 1-D mesh), as a phi face
no x3f(m,k+1).  CPU outputs and CLEAN lines bitwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
