From 71be376e3c541bc2a970477006f5f35111b7c93f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jingze Ma <jingzema0211@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 06:09:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] coordinates: the spherical-polar hydro source reads no x2
 flux at j+1 on a 1-D mesh

The hydro's uflx.x2f has ncells2 = 1 rows on a 1-D mesh; SrcTermsSphericalPolarHydro
read uflx.x2f(m,IM3,k,j+1,i) there (Kokkos bounds check, g3_pulsew: index [0,3,0,1,i] of
extents [1,5,1,1,260]; the read hit the zero IEN row).  On 1-D it now reads row j (the
x2 fluxes are zero there): the same value, bitwise.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/coordinates/coordinates.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/coordinates/coordinates.cpp b/src/coordinates/coordinates.cpp
index d327c9994..b5c594886 100644
--- a/src/coordinates/coordinates.cpp
+++ b/src/coordinates/coordinates.cpp
@@ -1613,6 +1613,8 @@ void Coordinates::SrcTermsSphericalPolarHydro(const DvceArray5D<Real> &w0,
